WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
A pulse of nitrate enters seawater containing a seaweed.
Gold parcels represent nitrate-N and are enlarged for visibility.

00:10.000 --> 00:16.000
Before nitrate can cross a membrane,
it must reach the seaweed surface.

00:16.000 --> 00:22.000
Individual ions wander in all directions.
They do not move deliberately towards the seaweed.

00:22.000 --> 00:27.000
Uptake removes nitrate at the surface.
Nearby water becomes depleted; diffusion supplies more.

00:27.000 --> 00:32.000
A concentration boundary layer develops.
It is a region of water, with molecules still moving.

00:32.000 --> 00:44.000
Watch a concentration gradient develop.
In this local model, bulk concentration is held constant.

00:44.000 --> 00:50.000
Bulk concentration is not surface concentration.
Delivery balances removal while the surface stays depleted.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
Switch uptake off. Keep diffusion running.
The depleted water refills and the concentration profile flattens.

01:00.000 --> 01:08.000
Restore uptake. Keep bulk nitrate and uptake capacity unchanged.
Predict what stronger water movement should change, and explain why.
